# ═══ WHAT RUNS ON LINUX IS STORED AND CHECKED OUT AS LF ═══
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true on the Windows machines this repository is developed
# on, so every text file is rewritten to CRLF on checkout. For a `.ts` file that
# is invisible. For a file that a Linux kernel executes it is not:
#
#   · a shell script with CRLF line endings fails at its shebang or at the
#     first `set -o pipefail`, with an error that names neither — `bash` sees
#     `pipefail\r` and says it is not a valid option;
#   · the deploy does `git reset --hard`, so the VPS gets exactly what the
#     checkout rules produce. A script that works locally and is broken there
#     is the worst version of this, because it is discovered during a deploy;
#   · a multi-line assertion against a repository file passes on Linux CI and
#     fails on a Windows checkout about a file neither machine changed. This
#     programme has already lost time to that twice.
#
# Only the file types where the ending is load-bearing are pinned. A blanket
# `* text=auto` would renormalise the whole tree in one commit, which is a
# large diff for a small problem and hides the next real change inside it.

# Shell scripts: executed by Linux, by cron and by the deploy.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf

# SQL the migration runner and psql read, including the tenant template whose
# content is compared byte for byte by the schema-parity checks.
*.sql           text eol=lf

# Container and CI definitions, read by Linux tooling.
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf

# Generated artefacts that a `--check` compares against a fresh render. The
# comparison is on bytes, so an ending rewritten on checkout reports a stale
# artefact for a file nobody touched.
*.cjs           text eol=lf

# Binary, so nothing tries.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.webp          binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.ttf           binary
*.otf           binary
*.mp4           binary
*.zip           binary
*.gz            binary
